From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Leonardo Bornia <leonardo.bornia@toradex.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 10:50:19 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] net: stmmac: qcom-ethqos: undo the SerDes power-up on failure

When phy_power_on() or phy_set_speed() fails in
qcom_ethqos_serdes_powerup(), the PHY is left initialized and powered
on: the PHY core keeps its supply enabled, and stmmac does not call
.serdes_powerdown() after a failed .serdes_powerup(). Every failed open
leaks one regulator enable, which shows up as _regulator_put() warnings
when the module is unloaded.

Power the PHY off and exit it on the error paths.

Upstream-Status: Pending
Signed-off-by: Leonardo Bornia <leonardo.bornia@toradex.com>
---
 .../ethernet/stmicro/stmmac/dwmac-qcom-ethqos.c    | 14 ++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/net/ethernet/stmicro/stmmac/dwmac-qcom-ethqos.c b/drivers/net/ethernet/stmicro/stmmac/dwmac-qcom-ethqos.c
index 3eca477bf..9858306ab 100644
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/stmicro/stmmac/dwmac-qcom-ethqos.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/stmicro/stmmac/dwmac-qcom-ethqos.c
@@ -775,9 +775,19 @@ static int qcom_ethqos_serdes_powerup(struct net_device *ndev, void *priv)
 
 	ret = phy_power_on(ethqos->serdes_phy);
 	if (ret)
-		return ret;
+		goto err_phy_exit;
+
+	ret = phy_set_speed(ethqos->serdes_phy, ethqos->serdes_speed);
+	if (ret)
+		goto err_phy_power_off;
+
+	return 0;
 
-	return phy_set_speed(ethqos->serdes_phy, ethqos->serdes_speed);
+err_phy_power_off:
+	phy_power_off(ethqos->serdes_phy);
+err_phy_exit:
+	phy_exit(ethqos->serdes_phy);
+	return ret;
 }
 
 static int ethqos_mac_finish_serdes(struct net_device *ndev, void *priv,
